# Liquid glass rather than blur, on every swaypplet surface: the
# compositor refracts its own composited output, so what bends behind a
# card is the actual window under it, not a stand-in. Window effects
# skip layer-shell surfaces entirely, which is why each namespace needs
# a block of its own — theme/glass-config.nix emits one per row of its
# `sessionSurfaces` table, and that table is where a surface is added,
# given a geometry, or explained.
#
# Nothing about the material belongs in this file. The greeter's
# compositor imports the same generator, and a number written here would
# apply to one of the two. patches/scenefx-liquid-glass.patch adds the
# render pass, patches/swayfx-liquid-glass.patch exposes it here.
#
# No shadows on these surfaces: depth comes from the hairline border
# (see the glass-card notes in swaypplet's style.css).
#
# swaypplet's settings pane edits the same material live over IPC
